2026-10-27 — v0.3 HISTORICAL VALIDATION CORRECTION
==================================================

WHY v0.2 FAILED
---------------
User run returned:
  RR F3/F2 max change = 0.746
  hard E^-1 F2/F1 effect = 1.329
  RR figure-shape log-RMS = 0.448
so the RR gate correctly failed.

Audit of v0.2 found three implementation problems:
1. The tau->nu_tau decay kernel used only the leptonic g0,g1 polynomial.
   The historical Dutta-Reno-Sarcevic/Rakshit-Reya calculation uses the full
   inclusive tau decay mixture: e, mu, pi, rho, a1 and multiprong X.
2. The historical published fluxes combine nu and antinu, while v0.2 only
   propagated neutrinos.
3. The v0.2 "Picard" iteration was not the RR Z iteration and therefore its
   2nd/3rd-iteration convergence could not be compared to RR's published
   convergence statement.

v0.3 CORRECTIONS
----------------
A. Full inclusive tau->nu_tau decay distribution implemented from DRS PRD 62,
   123001 Appendix A/Table I.  Normalization is unit tested for P=+/-1.

B. Historical validation now precomputes and propagates separate neutrino and
   antineutrino LHAPDF tables, with tau- P=-1 and tau+ P=+1, and combines them
   only at the final observable level.

C. RRZIterator replaces the ad hoc v0.2 Picard solver.  It uses a decay-aware
   Z^(0), then iterates the actual NC and tau-decay source/F ratios in the
   effective-Z ansatz.  The direct stepwise transport solver remains separate,
   providing an independent numerical cross-check of Z^(2).

D. The unreliable hand-entered Fig. 8 anchor RMS gate was removed.  It is
   replaced by published physics statements:
     * |F3/F2 - 1| < 5% for relevant bins;
     * the second iteration is non-negligible for hard E^-1;
     * direct solver agrees with Z2;
     * hard E^-1 has the 10^4-10^5 GeV regeneration bump;
     * E^-2 has no comparable bump.

E. DRS gate now uses their explicit historical quantitative statement:
   for vertical E^-1 at 1 PeV, nu_tau is about 6% and nu_mu/e about 1% of
   incident flux, with broad ranges retained because CT18NLO is not CTEQ5.

F. DRS Eq. (5), B [F_nutau - F_numu], is retained as an independent approximate
   secondary-flux check against the direct polarized tau-decay calculation.

BSM calculations remain blocked until BOTH RR and DRS gates pass.

