2026-10-27 — v0.4 ICECUBE EVENT-WEIGHTED OBSERVABILITY STAGE
=============================================================

INPUT STATUS
------------
The user's v0.3 run passed the combined historical validation gate:
  * Rakshit-Reya: PASS
  * Dutta-Reno-Sarcevic: PASS
The subsequent v0.3 BSM flux scan also passed its 5% distortion gate.

DETECTOR DATA CHOICE
--------------------
v0.4 uses the official IceCube public release accompanying
  M. G. Aartsen et al., Phys. Rev. D 91, 022001 (2015),
641 days of contained events above 1 TeV.

Official data-release URL:
https://icecube.wisc.edu/data-releases/2015/02/search-for-contained-neutrino-events-at-energies-greater-than-1-tev-in-2-years-of-data/

The release provides `effective_area.nu_tau.txt` in true neutrino-energy and
zenith bins.  IceCube states that the quoted total effective area is an average
for neutrinos and antineutrinos and is to be multiplied by their summed flux.

FLUX USED
---------
Per-flavor nu+nubar astrophysical best fit from the same 2015 analysis:
  Phi0 = 2.06e-18 GeV^-1 cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 at 100 TeV
  gamma = 2.46
restricted to the quoted fit interval 25 TeV -- 1.4 PeV.

CRITICAL EARTH-ATTENUATION TREATMENT
------------------------------------
The published IceCube effective area already contains the Standard-Model
zenith-dependent Earth attenuation.  Therefore v0.4 does NOT multiply Aeff by
the transmitted flux again.  It reweights the published Aeff by

  R_prop(E,theta) = T_BSM / T_SM

for upgoing bins.  Downgoing bins have R_prop=1.

DETECTOR-INTERACTION TREATMENT
------------------------------
The same BSM interaction can also change the probability to interact inside
IceCube.  The public total Aeff does not separate CC and NC acceptance weights,
so v0.4 reports:
  1. propagation-only counts/significance;
  2. propagation + detector proxy, where Aeff is additionally reweighted by
     the inclusive (sigma_CC + sigma_NC)_BSM / SM ratio.

This second quantity is explicitly a detector-response proxy, not yet the final
CC/NC/topology likelihood.

NEUTRINO / ANTINEUTRINO CORRECTION
----------------------------------
v0.4 generates and propagates nu_tau and antinu_tau separately, then combines
equal incident fluxes.  It also corrects a sign-convention issue retained as an
open caveat in v0.3: a diagonal neutrino charge-radius contribution has the
same relative interference sign for neutrino and antineutrino scattering.
The antineutrino cross section still differs through the usual chiral
kinematics; no extra manual BSM coupling sign flip is applied.

STATISTICAL DIAGNOSTICS
-----------------------
For every BSM model v0.4 writes:
  * total SM and BSM expected counts;
  * fractional total count shift;
  * fixed-flux Poisson Asimov significance;
  * significance after profiling an overall flux normalization;
  * significance after profiling normalization AND spectral index;
  * propagation-only versions of the first two;
  * a clearly labelled 7.5-year sqrt(exposure) projection using the same 2015
    acceptance (diagnostic only, NOT a reproduction of the later HESE sample);
  * exposure required for nominal 2 sigma and 3 sigma at fixed response.

The final observability judgment should use the normalization+tilt-profiled
quantity, not the raw fixed-flux significance.

