  Gen2 10 yr x10 projected Z = 0.6782
  area multiplier needed for 2 sigma in 10 yr = 86.97
  dominant profiled information energy = 2.371e5 GeV

Thus IceCube and simple Gen2 exposure scaling fail.

WHY ARCA IS TESTED DIFFERENTLY
------------------------------
The 2024 full-ARCA simulation provides two complementary selected samples:
  cosmic-neutrino tracks:  220/year for the paper's reference E^-2 flux
  cosmic-neutrino showers:  60/year for the same flux.

For a tau-specific interaction, the high-statistics nu_mu CC track sample is
essentially BSM-insensitive and can constrain the common astrophysical flux
normalisation and spectral index.  The BSM effect resides mainly in the
shower sample and, for Earth propagation, in its upgoing/down-going contrast.

This is a stronger nuisance-control strategy than the previous IceCube
tau-effective-area-only fold.

PUBLIC RESPONSE STATUS
----------------------
The 2024 ARCA paper states that the generated/analysed datasets and code are
public at Zenodo record 10949703.  v0.6 automatically downloads that record and
writes a complete file inventory.

However, v0.6 does NOT silently guess an unknown Zenodo table schema.  Until an
exact machine-readable response is positively identified, the numerical gate
uses a coarse digitisation of published Fig.7(b,c), calibrated separately to
the exact Table-1/2 cosmic rates (220 track and 60 shower events/year).

This makes the result reproducible and normalization-anchored, while honestly
retaining a response-shape systematic.

ARCA RESPONSE USED
------------------
Fig.7(c) shower components:
  * nu_e CC (+ Glashow, outside our main 25 TeV--1.4 PeV interval)
  * nu_tau CC shower decay
  * all-flavour NC
with separate upgoing and downgoing curves.

Fig.7(b) control sample:
  nu_mu CC tracks in four cos(theta) bins.

For equal astrophysical flavor fluxes:
  * nu_e CC is unaffected by the tau-only BSM interaction;
  * nu_tau CC is modified by Earth propagation only;
  * only the tau one-third of the all-flavour NC component is modified by
    tau propagation and the BSM NC detector cross section;
  * nu_mu CC tracks are used as an unaffected normalization/slope control.

STATISTICAL GATE
----------------
The likelihood profiles one common astrophysical normalization and spectral
index, first using showers alone and then using tracks+showers.

The present ARCA gate is deliberately SIGNAL-ONLY: published atmospheric
background rates are not yet available bin-by-bin in the fallback response.
Therefore it is an OPTIMISTIC UPPER BOUND on achievable significance.

Decision logic:
  * if even tracks+showers signal-only gives Z < 2, ARCA cannot rescue the
    benchmark and no background refinement can reverse that conclusion;
  * if Z >= 2, exact Zenodo response and binned backgrounds become mandatory
    before any positive claim.

The already-passed Rakshit-Reya / Dutta-Reno-Sarcevic transport validation is
unchanged.

